Local changes Copyright (C) 2026 Yeo Kheng Meng
Test-only: gives QEMU's usb-net a High Speed descriptor set (property
highspeed=on: bulk wMaxPacketSize 512, interrupt bInterval 9) beside the
Full Speed one, so the device attaches at 480 Mb/s on usb-ehci and on
qemu-xhci's USB 2 ports (12 Mb/s on UHCI); adds idvendor=/idproduct=
overrides; makes the ECM end-of-frame (short packet / ZLP) rule use the
endpoint's own wMaxPacketSize instead of a fixed 64; registers
usb_desc_attach so the speed's descriptor set is chosen at attach; and
fixes the RNDIS status endpoint, which copied its 8 bytes before NAKing:
EHCI retries the same USBPacket after a NAK, the bytes accumulated, and
QEMU aborted in usb_packet_copy (assertion) once RNDIS ran on usb-ehci. Applies to
official QEMU v11.1.0 hw/usb/dev-network.c. Build: x86_64-softmmu only,
--disable-slirp (the guest's netdev is a dgram socket joined to a stock
QEMU's user network, see 2026-10-22-cdcnet-9x.md). The emulator as a
whole remains GPL-2.0-or-later; dev-network.c keeps its upstream notice.
